# Publish

When the user says `publish`, commit the work from this chat, push it to `main`, and confirm the Brimble deploy. Do that in this turn. Do not stop after printing a commit title.

## Commit

Commit only files this chat changed. Leave other dirty files unstaged.

Follow the git commit format: lowercase `scope(area): short summary.` with a period. The message is the subject line only. Do not add a body. Do not add `Co-authored-by`.

If this chat changed nothing, say so and stop. Do not create an empty commit, and do not push.

## Push

The branch must be `main`. If it is not, stop and say so. Do not merge, rebase, or force-push.

Push with `git push origin main`.

## Deploy

The site is the Brimble project `docs` (`blnkfinance/blnk-docs` on `main`). The push starts the deploy. Do not run `brimble deploy`. That starts a second one.

Follow the deploy the push started:

```bash
brimble logs build docs
```

Wait until it finishes. The deploy succeeded when that commit's status is `ACTIVE`. `FAILED` means it is not published. Say the result, including the failure when it failed.

```text
# ❌ BAD — title only, or a second deploy
docs(core): update the quick start tabs.
brimble deploy

# ✅ GOOD — commit, push, then follow the git deploy
git push origin main
brimble logs build docs
```
